<section class="record-learning section" id="real-cases" aria-labelledby="real-cases-title" data-reading-milestone="real-cases">
    <div class="container record-learning__body">
        <span class="eyebrow">Real record investigations · identifying details omitted</span>
        <h2 id="real-cases-title">Start with a question like yours.</h2>
        <p class="record-learning__lede">See how we found original records and turned them into clear explanations. Explore the searches, document comparisons and findings behind our work. The findings are free to read.</p>
        @template.tags.recordFindingVisual(variant = "anderson")
        <div class="record-learning__pair">
            <article>
                <span class="eyebrow">Finding a layout · Roane County, TN</span>
                <h3>Where were the tank and drain field drawn?</h3>
                <p>We found the historical agency file behind the property listing: a three-bedroom design, a 900-gallon tank and three field lines. The original sketch gave the owner a documented starting point for understanding the layout.</p>
                <a href="/septic-as-built-records/#layout-case" data-track-click="nav" data-track-source-context="case_collection_layout" data-track-target-type="case_study">Follow the search and read the real drawing →</a>
            </article>
            <article>
                <span class="eyebrow">Recovering a missing file · Shelby County, TN</span>
                <h3>What can I give a buyer when I have no septic file?</h3>
                <p>We followed the County record route, obtained the source packet and turned the approved plan into a readable explanation the owner could share alongside the original pages.</p>
                <a href="/septic-record-brief-example/#sale-case" data-track-click="nav" data-track-source-context="case_collection_sale" data-track-target-type="case_study">See the source pages and finished explanation →</a>
            </article>
            <article>
                <span class="eyebrow">Comparing records · Anderson County, SC</span>
                <h3>The permit says 300 feet. What does the final record show?</h3>
                <p>We compared the planned design with the final installation record and highlighted the different recorded lengths. The result brought the recorded trench layout, tank size and design flow together in one guide.</p>
                <a href="/septic-permit-process/#design-final-case" data-track-click="nav" data-track-source-context="case_collection_final" data-track-target-type="case_study">Read what the two documents actually said →</a>
            </article>
            <article>
                <span class="eyebrow">Reviewing revised records · St. Croix County, WI</span>
                <h3>Can the old file explain my system before an addition?</h3>
                <p>We selected the relevant revised pages from the archive packet and explained the recorded system design, layout and capacity figures. The customer received a focused three-page extract with an explanation.</p>
                <a href="/septic-tank-location-records/#addition-file-case" data-track-click="nav" data-track-source-context="case_collection_addition" data-track-target-type="case_study">See how we made the archive packet useful →</a>
            </article>
            <article>
                <span class="eyebrow">Searching older records · Overton County, TN</span>
                <h3>Can earlier owner and road names uncover an older file?</h3>
                <p>Earlier owner and road clues led to a 1993 repair file, but it lacked the modern street number. We disclosed the possible connection without presenting it as a confirmed property match.</p>
                <a href="/septic-permit-search-by-address/#old-address-case" data-track-click="nav" data-track-source-context="case_collection_address" data-track-target-type="case_study">Follow the clues to the repair record →</a>
            </article>
        </div>
        <p class="record-learning__note">Each story identifies the records reviewed and explains their scope. Historical documents are a starting point for any needed on-site or project review.</p>
        <div class="record-learning__next">
            <div><h3>What do you need to know about your property?</h3><p>Send the address and your question. Research and agency requests are free. Review the scope of relevant findings before choosing the original records and detailed answers for US $29. Agency fees are additional at cost, with your approval.</p></div>
            <a class="button button--primary" href="/offer-prep-septic-file-check/#record-help" data-record-help-cta data-track-click="nav" data-track-source-context="case_collection_request" data-track-target-type="lead_form">Ask about my property</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
